          "note": "Figma 81:801 lays the trail out as a row, centred, with a 4px gap and hug sizing. The Figma Desktop frame shows six levels (Level 1 to 5 and the active one); the fixture raises maxVisible to 6 so none is collapsed. The fixture is 435px wide, the width of the Figma export, because the component fills its container instead of hugging its content. `responsive` is off so the 435px fixture keeps the desktop trail (the component switches to the back link by width). No whole-trail pixel diff: measured on the 2x exports, the label starts of this render trail Figma's by 1, 2, 2, 3 and 3 device pixels over five items (about 0.5 CSS px per item). Figma sizes each hugged label to a whole-pixel text width, a browser keeps the fractional width, so the error grows along the trail while every box, gap and style matches exactly (style parity). The chevron and icon glyphs also differ: Figma draws them from their own 16px drawings, mud-icon scales one 24px drawing. The single-item mobile state compares pixels (0.29%)."
